OL,3,GNEWSAJohn Swinney defends #45,000
OL,4,Abusiness-class flights to World Cup
OL,5,
OL,6,FJohn Swinney has defended the use of
OL,7,Fmore than #45,000 of public funds on
OL,8,Fbusiness-class flights for him and two
OL,9,Fsenior aides to the World Cup.
OL,11,FScotland's first minister flew to
OL,12,FBoston on 11 June for Scotland's
OL,13,Fopening match, before taking part in
OL,14,Ftrade talks in Kentucky three days
OL,15,Flater.
OL,17,FWhile he and two senior officials
OL,18,Ftravelled business class, Sports
OL,19,FMinister Maree Todd and several other
OL,20,Fofficials went to the US on
OL,21,Fsignificantly cheaper economy-class
OL,22,Fflights.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,427,420,260,160,0,100
